  "consumed": "Juice Primary",
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1,000eb (Very Expensive) per dose<br>\n<strong>Type:</strong> Street Drug</p>\n<p>Primary (1 month): take 1d6 Humanity Loss; it takes a full 24 hours of doing nothing else to administer, and never in combat. BODY +3, which does raise HP and Death Save and stacks with cyberware. A second dose in the same month is an overdose: immediate hospitalization and Addiction Therapy. No effect on FBCs or users with Internal Linear Frames. You get outbursts of rage. Secondary (DV29): addiction. While addicted: COOL -2 and REF -1 (minimum 1); when not on Juice, you crave it and BODY and MOVE -2 (minimum 1). Rapidetox ends the Primary Effect only; the addiction needs Addiction Therapy.</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>While addicted, switch on the \"Juice Addiction\" effect.</li>\n<li>When an addicted character doses, use \"Juice Addicted Primary\" instead of the normal primary effect; it cancels the withdrawal penalties for the duration.</li>\n<li>Stat and skill changes are automated; caps, minimums, durations, and everything else are not.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Gear, Drugs, &amp; Frames &gt; Consumables &gt; Street Drugs).</em></p>"
  },
